** TEST SUCCEEDED **

What each bound proves:

- AtCapMinusOne (16 MiB - 1) accepted: echoes image(16777215B.png→w1:p2); no note.
- AtCap (16 MiB exact) accepted: echoes image(16777216B.png→w1:p2); FFI enforces >, not >=.
- OverCap (16 MiB + 1) rejected: inputNote = writeFailed("endpoint byte budget exceeded")
  until outboundByteLimit lifted (see configuration note); nothing reaches the wire.
- SendWritesTheGoldenFrame: FFI-captured golden frame is byte-exact vs the live send.
- RejectsOversizeSourceBeforeDecode: readCapped aborts mid-read, never retains the file.
- StripsEXIFByDefault: source UserComment + GPS absent on the PNG re-encode
  (the synthesized dimension-only EXIF dict that ImageIO writes for PNG is
  re-encoded-pixel metadata, not carried-over source metadata — asserted on
  UserComment/GPS markers).
- StripsCorruptEXIF: malformed APP1 segment → ImageIO drops it; no carry-over.
- DownscalePath: 512-pixel noise PNG over the 300 KiB cap requests downscale;
  256-pixel re-encode fits and is reported at the chosen pixel size.
- ReadCappedEnforcesCapDuringLoad: 5 KiB file with 1 KiB cap → exceedsCap
  the moment the running total crosses, not after a full read.

The outbound byte budget is lifted to 24 MiB at model connect time
(HerdrClientConfig.outboundByteLimit) so a max-size clipboard image plus its
frame envelope fits the queue; the FFI default 4 MiB silently rejected them
as "endpoint byte budget exceeded" before this configuration was added
(see learnings: "Outbound byte budget blocks max-size clipboard images").

